# /etc/iptables/rules.v4 for an origin host — the INPUT chain every origin
# shares, and the shape infra/firewall/cloudflare-only.sh expects: accept
# replies, ICMP, loopback, SSH and 80/443, reject everything else. It is the
# OCI VM's INPUT (minus fail2ban's own jumps), written down so a fresh host
# can be given the same one.
#
# Boot-time only. netfilter-persistent loads this file at boot, before Docker
# starts and adds its chains. Never load it into a running host with
# `iptables-restore`: that flushes the whole filter table, Docker's chains
# with it. infra/firewall/apply-baseline.sh applies the same INPUT rules live,
# one `iptables -A` at a time, and installs this file with --persist.
#
# No FORWARD or OUTPUT rules on purpose: Docker owns FORWARD (it sets the
# policy to DROP and adds its chains when it starts).
#
# Runbook: docs/how-to/lock-origin-to-cloudflare.md, "Onboard another origin
# host". Tests: __tests__/nest/infra/firewall.test.ts.
*filter
:INPUT ACCEPT [0:0]
:FORWARD ACCEPT [0:0]
:OUTPUT ACCEPT [0:0]
-A INPUT -m state --state RELATED,ESTABLISHED -j ACCEPT
-A INPUT -p icmp -j ACCEPT
-A INPUT -i lo -j ACCEPT
-A INPUT -p tcp -m state --state NEW -m tcp --dport 22 -j ACCEPT
-A INPUT -p tcp -m state --state NEW -m tcp --dport 443 -j ACCEPT
-A INPUT -p tcp -m state --state NEW -m tcp --dport 80 -j ACCEPT
-A INPUT -j REJECT --reject-with icmp-host-prohibited
COMMIT
